}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Bayara}}|area_km2=20,972|population_census=5,716,926|population_census_year=2025|regional_languages=|common_languages=[[w:Aragonese language|Xacano]], [[Andalusian language|Andalusian]], [[Baliscano]]|cctld=.xra|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}}|ethnic_groups_year=2024|ethnic_groups=86.8% [[Baliscans]] <br> 13.2% [[Ethnography of Balisca|others]]|mapsize=290|population_census_rank=7th}}'''Xaraba''' ([[Bayani]]: خَرَابَة ''Ḥarāba''; {{Literal translation|badlands|wilds}}) is a coastal region in western [[Bayara]], and one of the [[regions of Balisca|seven regions of the community]]. It borders [[Marjcorzo]] to the north, [[Llaragón]] to the east, and [[Carpinchera]] and [[Camaca]] to the south and southwest. 

Xaraba is almost entirely within the east [[Western Plains (Balisca)|Bayaran coastal plain]], and generally consists of lowland plains and low hills. The northwest remainder of the state consists of the Bayaran Delta. The region has a {{W|humid subtropical climate}}, characterized by hot, humid summers and mild to cool winters. 

